# Sample entries, so the carousel can be seen working before there is
# anything real to put in it.
#
# These are NOT testimonials. The names are placeholders and the quotes are
# written to demonstrate layout — a short one, a long one, one with a role
# and one without — not to stand in for anyone's opinion. Nothing in this
# file renders on the live page: the reader only ever loads
# testimonials.yaml, and only entries there marked `verified: true` appear.
#
# To preview the section with these:
#
#     /?preview=testimonials
#
# Every card is watermarked "sample" in that mode, and the mode is ignored
# unless this example file exists. Copy a real one into testimonials.yaml
# when you have it, set verified: true, and the section becomes real.

testimonials:
  - quote: >-
      A short one, to show how the card looks when somebody said something
      brief and there is a lot of white space left over.
    name: Sample Name
    role: Placeholder role
    verified: true

  - quote: >-
      A longer one, which is the more common case and the harder layout
      problem: it runs to three or four lines, wraps past the avatar, and
      still has to sit level with the shorter cards beside it without
      anybody noticing the difference in height.
    name: Second Sample
    role: Another placeholder
    verified: true

  - quote: >-
      A third, with no role attached, because not everyone wants one shown
      and the card must not look broken when the line is missing.
    name: Third Sample
    verified: true
